---
import Page from "@layouts/Page.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro";
import SectionHead from "@components/SectionHead.astro";
import SectionSub from "@components/SectionSub.astro";
import Organizations from "@components/Organizations.astro";
const title = "About Me";
const subtitle = "Strategy, accessibility, and hands-on execution for content-driven web platforms.";
---

<Page title={title} subtitle={subtitle}>
  <slot slot="HeadMeta">
    <title>About Chris Kraft | Senior Front-End Engineer</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Chris Kraft — senior front-end engineer building accessible, content-driven web platforms, from web architecture and content strategy through production." />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Chris Kraft, senior front-end engineer, web architecture, web accessibility, UX strategy, content architecture, WordPress, Astro, WCAG" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="About Chris Kraft" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Senior front-end engineer building accessible, content-driven web platforms — web architecture, content strategy, and production front-end." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="profile" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://kriggity.com/about/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="About Chris Kraft" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Senior front-end engineer building accessible, content-driven web platforms — architecture, content strategy, and production front-end." />
  </slot>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="My Background" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>I'm a <strong>Senior Front-End Engineer</strong> with 27+ years of experience building <strong>accessible, content-driven web platforms</strong>. My work focuses on <strong>experience architecture, front-end engineering, and CMS strategy</strong>, with an emphasis on <strong>usability, performance, and long-term maintainability</strong>.</p>
        <p>I've partnered with agencies, product teams, and public-sector organizations to define goals, clarify <strong>content structure</strong>, and establish <strong>technical direction</strong> before moving into production. I'm most effective in roles where I can help determine <strong>what to build, why it matters, and then build it</strong>.</p>
        <p>Much of my work centers on <strong>WordPress platform architecture</strong>, where I design <strong>scalable content models, editorial workflows, and front-end systems</strong> that support real-world publishing needs. <strong>Accessibility and <abbr title="Web Content Accessibility Guidelines">WCAG</abbr>-aligned practices</strong> are embedded into my approach from the start, ensuring platforms work well for both users and the teams that maintain them.</p>
        <p>While I'm comfortable contributing across the full project lifecycle, my strengths sit at the intersection of <strong><abbr title="user experience">UX</abbr> strategy, content architecture, and front-end development</strong>—collaborating with designers, engineers, and stakeholders to deliver <strong>production-ready, sustainable web solutions</strong>.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="How I Work" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>My work starts with understanding the problem space—business goals, user needs, content constraints, and technical realities. From there, I define <strong>experience architecture</strong>, including content structure, user flows, accessibility requirements, and technical direction.</p>
        <p>Once direction is set, I move quickly into <strong>hands-on implementation</strong>. I build <strong>production-ready front ends and CMS platforms</strong> with a focus on <strong>accessibility, performance, and maintainability</strong>.</p>
        <p>I work comfortably across strategy and execution, either independently or embedded within cross-functional teams. I prioritize clear decisions, steady progress, and systems that continue to hold up long after launch.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="What I Focus On" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty flex flex-col gap-8">
        <div>
          <h3>UX Strategy & Experience Architecture</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Defining structure, flows, and interaction patterns that support real user and business needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Front-End Engineering</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Building accessible, scalable front ends using modern HTML, CSS, and JavaScript practices.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>WordPress Platform Architecture</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Designing content models, templates, and editorial workflows that scale and reduce friction.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Accessibility</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Embedding <abbr title="Web Content Accessibility Guidelines">WCAG</abbr>-aligned practices into structure and implementation—not treating accessibility as an afterthought.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Long-Term Sustainability</h3>
          <p class="mt-0">Creating systems that are understandable, maintainable, and built to evolve over time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Who I Work With" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>I've worked with agencies, product teams, nonprofits, and public-sector organizations—often on <strong>content-heavy platforms</strong> where clarity, accessibility, and governance matter as much as visual presentation.</p>
        <p>I partner closely with designers, developers, content strategists, and stakeholders to align goals and translate them into <strong>durable technical solutions</strong>. I'm particularly effective in environments that value collaboration, ownership, and practical problem-solving over performative process.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="What You Can Expect" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p class="mb-[1lh]">When you work with me, you can expect:</p>
        <ul class="formatted mb-8">
          <li>Clear thinking and honest communication</li>
          <li>A focus on structure and systems, not surface-level polish</li>
          <li>Accessibility and usability built in from the start</li>
          <li>Thoughtful technical decisions grounded in real constraints</li>
          <li>Solutions designed to last—not just launch</li>
        </ul>
        <p>I bring a steady, pragmatic approach to complex problems, with an emphasis on doing the right work in the right order.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Let's Talk About What You're Building" />
    <SectionSub>
      <div class="text-pretty">
        <p>If you're looking for someone who can help define what to build, translate that direction into working systems, and see it through to production, <a href="mailto:chris.kraft@kriggity.com" target="_blank">I'm always open to a conversation</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </SectionSub>
  </Section>
  <Section>
    <SectionHead title="Organizations I've Worked With" />
    <Organizations />
  </Section>
</Page>
